#: index.docbook:538
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>New Screen Session</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:540
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Open a new session</action> with the <application>Screen</"
"application> virtual terminal manager. See <userinput><command>man</command> "
"<option>screen</option> </userinput>for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:544
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This menu entry will only be visible if Screen (<command>screen</command>) "
"is installed on your system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:550
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Close Tab</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:552
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>Close</action> the current tab and the session within."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:557
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Quit</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:559
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Quit</action> &konsole;, closing all sessions and any applications "
"launched from them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:565
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also open a new session with a key shortcut. By default, <keycombo "
"action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>N</keycap></keycombo> is used. You can "
"also define your own key shortcuts through the "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure Shortcuts...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu command."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:571
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The list of available sessions will reflect what programs are installed "
"along with any user defined sessions. The session list will be alphabetized "
"for quick viewing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:575
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Finally, note that the session types can be modified, and new types created, "
"by using the configuration dialog, reached from the "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Manage Profiles...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu entry."
msgstr ""

